Bail out with a 404 when the requested path is not a valid internal path,
but not while an error page is being rendered.

Based on https://git.drupalcode.org/project/facets_pretty_paths/-/merge_requests/25
(https://www.drupal.org/project/facets_pretty_paths/issues/3575306), which
throws a NotFoundHttpException from the PrettyPathsActiveFilters constructor.
On a site with a language switcher block, the 404 page's subrequest keeps the
original invalid path and builds the facet URL processors, so the constructor
throws again and core starts another 404 subrequest. When the facet caches are
cold (the first request after a cache clear is a 404), every 404 recurses until
PHP runs out of memory. Skipping the check for exception subrequests keeps the
fix for paths like /events/x/y%20 and stops the loop.

--- a/src/PrettyPathsActiveFilters.php
+++ b/src/PrettyPathsActiveFilters.php
@@ -88,6 +88,16 @@
     $this->routeMatch = $routeMatch;
     $this->coderManager = $coderManager;
     $this->request = $requestStack->getCurrentRequest();
+    // Validate the current path. Skip this while rendering an error page:
+    // the 404/403 subrequest keeps the original invalid path, so throwing here
+    // would start another 404 subrequest, recursing until memory runs out.
+    $path = $this->request->getPathInfo();
+    $url_is_valid_internal = \Drupal::pathValidator()
+      ->getUrlIfValidWithoutAccessCheck($path);
+    if (!$url_is_valid_internal && !$this->request->attributes->has('exception')) {
+      // throw 404.
+      throw new \Symfony\Component\HttpKernel\Exception\NotFoundHttpException();
+    }
     $this->batchStorage = $batch_storage;
     $this->configFactory = $config_factory;
     $this->moduleHandler = $module_handler;
